<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zunyi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zunyi is a city in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guizhou">Guizhou</a> province in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. It grew around Bozhou, the domain ruled by the hereditary Yang chieftains from the 9th century until the Ming conquest in 1600. In January 1935 the Zunyi Conference held there during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/long-march">Long March</a> brought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mao-zedong">Mao Zedong</a> to the leadership of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chinese-communist-party">Chinese Communist Party</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zunyi.jpg" alt="Zunyi" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Augusthaiho · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E6%B0%91%E4%B8%BB%E8%B7%AF_7007.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
